{"id": "EUVD-2026-86836", "enisaUuid": "04a9fce2-e226-32d2-9233-f6a26c63348e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error\n\nqla_nvme_xmt_ls_rsp() obtains uctx, which was linked into\nfcport->unsol_ctx_head by qla2xxx_process_purls_iocb() and is still linked\nwhen the NVMe transport calls back to transmit the LS response. On the\nerror (out:) path the function frees uctx with kfree() but never removes\nit from the list. This leaves a freed node in fcport->unsol_ctx_head: the\nnext list_add_tail() for that fcport writes through the freed node, and a\nsubsequent list_del() can corrupt the list or panic.\n\nUnlink uctx with list_del() before kfree() on the error path, matching the\nother free sites in qla_nvme_release_lsrsp_cmd_kref() and\nqla2xxx_process_purls_pkt(). qla2x00_rel_sp() in the failure path only\nreturns the SRB to its pool and does not invoke sp->put_fn, so the out:\npath is the sole free and uctx is always still linked there.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:03", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/925a9129a514b7c3bc0a8af01e51868adbb9a83e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbbf1484496aac86038e67ac984949af58009d4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a95fc5f1c12bba1dbff72bd2611e7fad0758831b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c55d649a6cc246c3ccd5d118faea230c46b60f35", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e46160a5d4fa59bf4d5f3412b6b5cb79edb967dd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97528", "GHSA-cw7x-747c-3cx3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03d4e1e0-3681-3704-8c1c-f169be872dca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "2e2c5254-3ef7-3aad-899c-7436fb28635c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <cbbf1484496aac86038e67ac984949af58009d4b"}, {"id": "46444bff-4eb8-3cca-8d3f-a0876403badc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <e46160a5d4fa59bf4d5f3412b6b5cb79edb967dd"}, {"id": "4f0ba44a-b089-3428-8c63-76f6c4a565aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "4fc2a039-a013-35e8-9ed1-b71db9b69fb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "64f0db1a-5663-3de5-af09-9716db2563db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "8b994083-7606-36ba-b17f-7795db5f249b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a5fe3f09-54bc-31ec-b840-174a69368df9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <c55d649a6cc246c3ccd5d118faea230c46b60f35"}, {"id": "c0650e6a-53b0-32c0-80d8-c267164f4938", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <a95fc5f1c12bba1dbff72bd2611e7fad0758831b"}, {"id": "d007b4dc-a96a-34ea-8561-7d6f9d5ee277", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "e9069a90-0b57-3af6-820c-a04ff155caf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ff169569-b1cb-3c2d-95e8-94239969c494", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <925a9129a514b7c3bc0a8af01e51868adbb9a83e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "415eaa67-2a13-31d4-95b2-0cd1c4d5d6da", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}